class.description:
The Authentication plugin's singleton. Each service is set up in [b]Project Settings > Authentication[/b], a section each, with a block per platform for what differs (each platform's own client). [method sign_in_with] signs in with one: in the player's browser on a computer, in a window of its own in a web game. The game gets the service's token ([method get_token]) to call its API, and the player's account ([method get_account]), [code]"<service>:<id>"[/code] ([code]google:1102…[/code], [code]supabase:4bade…[/code]).
An online game needs nothing else: when its server asks for a login ([b]Project Settings > Online > Login > Check: Services[/b]), the token goes to [method Online.login] by itself, and the server checks it with this same plugin ([method check_token]).
[codeblock]
fn _on_sign_in_pressed() void {
	Authentication.sign_in_with("google")
}

on Authentication.signed_in(token: String, data: Dictionary) {
	print("Signed in as " + Authentication.get_account())
}

on Authentication.sign_in_failed(reason: String) {
	print("Could not sign in: " + reason)
}
[/codeblock]
